{"audio": "matthew-04.opus", "duration_ms": 196546, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 2080, "end_ms": 3480, "text": "Matthew, Chapter Four."}, {"start_ms": 4920, "end_ms": 9720, "text": "Then Jesus was led by the Spirit into the wilderness to be tempted by the devil."}, {"start_ms": 10660, "end_ms": 14260, "text": "After fasting forty days and forty nights, He was hungry."}, {"start_ms": 15280, "end_ms": 26801, "text": "The tempter came to Him and said, “If You are the Son of God, tell these stones to become bread.” But Jesus answered, “It is written: ‘Man shall not live on bread alone,"}, {"start_ms": 26901, "end_ms": 34921, "text": "but on every word that comes from the mouth of God.’” Then the devil took Him to the holy city and set Him on the pinnacle of the temple."}, {"start_ms": 36101, "end_ms": 39521, "text": "“If You are the Son of God,” he said, “throw Yourself down."}, {"start_ms": 39701, "end_ms": 57182, "text": "For it is written: ‘He will command His angels concerning You, and they will lift You up in their hands, so that You will not strike Your foot against a stone.’” Jesus replied, “It is also written: ‘Do not put the Lord your God to the test.’” Again,"}, {"start_ms": 57262, "end_ms": 62842, "text": "the devil took Him to a very high mountain and showed Him all the kingdoms of the world and their glory."}, {"start_ms": 63842, "end_ms": 71062, "text": "“All this I will give You,” he said, “if You will fall down and worship me.” “Away from Me, Satan!” Jesus told him."}, {"start_ms": 71422, "end_ms": 80382, "text": "“For it is written: ‘Worship the Lord your God and serve Him only.’” Then the devil left Him, and angels came and ministered to Him."}, {"start_ms": 82043, "end_ms": 86523, "text": "When Jesus heard that John had been imprisoned, He withdrew to Galilee."}, {"start_ms": 87363, "end_ms": 104083, "text": "Leaving Nazareth, He went and lived in Capernaum, which is by the sea in the region of Zebulun and Naphtali, to fulfill what was spoken through the prophet Isaiah: “Land of Zebulun and land of Naphtali, the Way of the Sea, beyond the Jordan,"}, {"start_ms": 104583, "end_ms": 118824, "text": "Galilee of the Gentiles— the people living in darkness have seen a great light; on those living in the land of the shadow of death, a light has dawned.” From that time on Jesus began to preach, “Repent,"}, {"start_ms": 119244, "end_ms": 130224, "text": "for the kingdom of heaven is near.” As Jesus was walking beside the Sea of Galilee, He saw two brothers, Simon called Peter and his brother Andrew."}, {"start_ms": 131004, "end_ms": 134224, "text": "They were casting a net into the sea, for they were fishermen."}, {"start_ms": 135124, "end_ms": 143104, "text": "“Come, follow Me,” Jesus said, “and I will make you fishers of men.” And at once they left their nets and followed Him."}, {"start_ms": 144044, "end_ms": 150005, "text": "Going on from there, He saw two other brothers, James son of Zebedee and his brother John."}, {"start_ms": 150665, "end_ms": 154305, "text": "They were in a boat with their father Zebedee, mending their nets."}, {"start_ms": 155045, "end_ms": 160205, "text": "Jesus called them, and immediately they left the boat and their father and followed Him."}, {"start_ms": 162025, "end_ms": 170965, "text": "Jesus went throughout Galilee, teaching in their synagogues, preaching the gospel of the kingdom, and healing every disease and sickness among the people."}, {"start_ms": 172045, "end_ms": 186206, "text": "News about Him spread all over Syria, and people brought to Him all who were ill with various diseases, those suffering acute pain, the demon-possessed, those having seizures, and the paralyzed, and He healed them."}, {"start_ms": 187386, "end_ms": 194426, "text": "Large crowds followed Him, having come from Galilee, the Decapolis, Jerusalem, Judea, and beyond the Jordan."}], "words": [{"t": "Matthew,", "s": 2080, "e": 2440, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 2800, "e": 3120, "si": 0}, {"t": "Four.", "s": 3